<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait credit extension up in October.</title>
<headline>Kuwait credit extension up in October.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Domestic credit extended by banks operating in Kuwait rose to 3.081 billion dinars at the end of October from 3.009 billion in September, Central Bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The credit amounted to 2.221 billion dinars at the end of October 1995.</p>
<p>Balance of cash portion used from domestic credit facilities by sector:</p>
<p>				Figures in million dinars</p>
<p>				     Oct '96	     Oct '95</p>
<p>Trade				511.4		  674.9</p>
<p>Industry			   252.0		  162.8</p>
<p>Construction		     194.0		  129.8</p>
<p>Agriculture and Fishing	 10.3		    7.9</p>
<p>Non-bank financial</p>
<p> institutions		    150.1		  119.0</p>
<p>Personal Facilities	  1,408.7		  636.3</p>
<p>Real Estate			381.0		  333.2</p>
<p>Other				173.5		  157.5</p>
<p>Total			    3,081.2		2,221.4</p>
<p> of which, consumer loans    521.2		  524.8</p>
<p>Note: Non-bank financial institutions include insurance, money exchange and investment firms. The figures include the effect of purchasing debts of Kuwaiti debtors in return for Debt Purchase Bonds since December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.303 dinars)</p>
</text>
